d_124f0:
        db '  help             this list, a page at a time', 10
        db '  NAME             (v2.9) an object', 39, 's name alone runs it; an app (NET, calc ...) opens', 10
        db '  kill NAME        close a program in a window by its name (v2.9)', 10
        db '  sentinel         check every system object against the build', 39, 's signed list (v2.9)', 10
        db '  sentinel trust NAME   run a CHANGED system object anyway, until the next start (admin)', 10
        db '  whoami           this machine', 39, 's identity: ID, role, generation, parent (v2.9.2)', 10
        db '  ls [all|DRAWER]  objects in the cabinet / everything / one drawer', 10
        db '  room [free]      the storage room: cabinet + drawers; free = unload idle ones', 10
        db '  drawer NAME      a new drawer for 63 more objects (maint)', 10
        db '  stow NAME DRAWER / unstow NAME   move an object into / out of a drawer (maint)', 10
        db '  id NAME          the object', 39, 's RGBA identity', 10
        db '  cores [test]     the CPU cores; test = a picture drawn by one core, then all', 10
        db '  update [GO]      what is new on a USB stick with a newer disk.img; GO = back up, then write it (maint)', 10
        db '  update back      the system as it was before the last update (maint; then it restarts)', 10
        db '  puffer [GO|CLONE]  make a USB stick that starts NinuxOS: GO = a fresh system, CLONE = this one', 10
        db '  files [cd NAME|get NAME]  a Windows / Mac / Linux pen drive (FAT32): list, folder, bring a file in', 10
        db '  spaces           META: the full-screen programs on this machine (Photon ...), pick one to start', 10
        db '  bench            one performance test of everything: processor, memory, screen, disk, cores (8 s)', 10
        db '  cores one|all    programs on the first core only (the default) / on every core', 10
        db '  cores solo       shared drawing work on the first core alone, on / off', 10
        db '  cores beat       three ', 39, 'alive', 39, ' squares at the top right, on / off', 10
        db '  pci              the devices on the PCI bus', 10
        db '  usb [on]         USB controllers; on = USB keyboard and mouse (xHCI)', 10
        db '  usb boot on|off  start USB at every boot (maint)', 10
        db '  mnt              look at the USB ports again: a stick put in after the start', 10
        db '  shot             keep the screen as a picture object (the PrtSc key does it anywhere)', 10
        db '  away             lock the screen until the administrator password (Ctrl + Alt + L anywhere)', 10
        db '  login on|off     ask the password at every start', 10
        db '  user [add NAME LEVEL | del NAME]  people: each a password and a level (maint)', 10
        db '  tune [auto|max|safe|min|off]  the processor', 39, 's clock: charts, turbo, a governor (', 39, 'tune x', 39, ' = help)', 10
        db '  uproot / root    move this whole system to another machine by a stick (', 39, 'uproot', 39, ' explains)', 10
        db '  build refresh keep media | discard media   back to a new build', 39, 's state (maint)', 10
        db '  colors [matrix|amber|paper|classic]  the shell', 39, 's colour scheme', 10
        db '  level [18|16|12|7|0]  ratings: the highest rating that opens on this machine (password)', 10
        db '  rate NAME N      an object', 39, 's rating: 0, 7, 12, 16, 18 (maint)', 10
        db '  gpu [on|cursor]  virtio-gpu: the GPU shows the screen; cursor = hardware pointer', 10
        db '  gpu trace on|off|save   record what the GPU driver does (the GPU lab)', 10
        db '  gpu probe        read-only: each display device, NVIDIA chip ID, engines, clock', 10
        db '  sgpu [test|bench|demo|photon|ptest|wc on|off]  the SUB-GPU: every core draws like a GPU', 10
        db '  machine          the processor, cores, memory, screen, graphics and disk', 10
        db '  sound / play [HZ MS | NAME]   the sound device / a tune, a tone, a sound object', 10
        db '  screen [W H|auto] the screen modes; W H = use that size from the next start (maint)', 10
        db '  net [on|ip A.B.C.D [MASK [GW]]]  the network (e1000; DHCP); ping A.B.C.D', 10
        db '  serve [on|off] / get A.B.C.D NAME [AS]   Meta Net: give / fetch shared objects', 10
        db '  share [NAME] / unshare NAME / look A.B.C.D   the public directory here / there', 10
        db '  send A.B.C.D NAME / serve inbox on|off   transfer an object / accept transfers', 10
        db '  subscribe / unsubscribe A.B.C.D / broadcast NAME   broadcasts to subscribers', 10
        db '  install [N ERASE] put NinuxOS on SATA disk N (erases it) - boot from it after', 10
        db '  meta NAME        show an object', 39, 's metadata', 10
        db '  view NAME        ASMO viewer: META, then DATA as text or hex', 10
        db '  NAME/TYPE        same name, pick by META type: view calc/source', 10
        db '  run NAME [SOCK]  call an object', 39, 's socket (default: first)', 10
        db '  desktop          the desktop; programs open side by side in windows (v1.14)', 10
        db '  echo TEXT        print text', 10
        db '  mem / memtest    memory map and allocator self-test', 10
        db '  uptime           time since boot', 10
        db '  log TEXT         write text to the serial log', 10
        db '  crash            test the crash screen', 10
        db '  sources          PyTon source objects and whether they are compiled', 10
        db '  build [NAME]     compile programs (type:script) to native objects (maint)', 10
        db '  maint            maintenance mode on/off (the cabinet can be changed)', 10
        db '  copy / rename / delete NAME ...   change the cabinet (maint)', 10
        db '  disk             boot disk, slots, gaps and free space', 10
        db '  scan [fix]       find every object by reading the disk; fix = list them again (maint)', 10
        db '  recover LBA NAME bring back a deleted object found by scan (maint)', 10
        db '  compact          close the gaps between objects (maint)', 10
        db '  hide / show NAME STATE 2: hidden from the desktop; show asks the admin password', 10
        db '  erase NAME       zero the object on disk and remove it - for good (maint)', 10
        db '  dropdata / cleandata / cleansockets NAME   empty or zero parts (maint)', 10
        db '  inject NAME SRC  put the DATA of SRC into NAME (maint)', 10
        db '  passwd           set or change the administrator password', 10
        db '  lock / unlock NAME   encrypt the DATA with a passphrase / decrypt it (maint)', 10
        db '  shutdown / restart  power off or restart (also the power button on the desktop)', 10
        db '  shield on|off|test  run objects in ring 3, protected from the kernel (v1.8)', 10
        db '  cls / info / version', 10, 0

d_13a47:
        db 'NinuxOS v2.9.59 with ASMO v4 objects (v2.9.50: Studio', 39, 's panel and tabs, a program as wallpaper, people; v2.9.49: NET on '
        db 'the whole screen, login, Phone; v2.9.48: install for UEFI, the screen above 4 GB, level strict; v2.9.47: move mode (Alt+'
        db 'M); an uprooted system is sealed, uproot BURN; v2.9.45: Copycat, games on the whole screen; v2.9.44: the Realtek network'
        db ' card, ratings; v2.9.43: colors; the UEFI start takes the biggest screen; v2.9.42: the UEFI start; v2.9.41: tune asks ev'
        db 'ery core; v2.9.40: mnt tries harder, games swap with the desktop, Shift marks text; v2.9.39: Alt + the Ngage key swaps a'
        db ' program and the desktop; a new look for Studio; v2.9.38: the chained record, uproot / root; v2.9.37: fastback - letters'
        db ' drawn from ready answers; v2.9.36: tune steers through Speed Shift, says who holds the processor back; v2.9.34: tune - '
        db 'the processor', 39, 's clock: turbo, charts, the EMA governor; v2.9.33: PrtSc, Ctrl+Alt+L, Ctrl keys, alarms, PyNamp / Search /'
        db ' Projector / Bags / Widgets; v2.9.32: mnt - a USB stick put in after the start; v2.9.31: security - maint asks the passw'
        db 'ord, only verified code runs on the kernel', 39, 's page tables; v2.9.30:the tools are a kernel suit (k_tools) - the extension '
        db 'has room again; v2.9.29: bench - one performance test; v2.9.28: Mail (name@ninux), search in Device; v2.9.27: every core'
        db ' gets its own stack at the start, Nest, Device; v2.9.26: update keeps a backup - update back returns to it; v2.9.25: eve'
        db 'ry start tries all cores again, cores says who does the shared work; v2.9.24: ASMONCRAFT, the first META game; v2.9.23: '
        db 'Interfacer - build a NET page with the mouse; v2.9.22: Paint - brush sizes and Undo; v2.9.21: META the launcher, a late '
        db 'core parks itself, labels centred; v2.9.20: menus over every window, Cyrillic in Notepad, a line a core in cores; v2.9.1'
        db '9: the letters are in every build now, EN / BG in the dock, the Windows key closes the menu; v2.9.18: files from FAT32 p'
        db 'en drives, WAV in play; v2.9.17: its own letters with Cyrillic, BG keyboard (Alt+Shift), the Windows key; v2.9.16: Puffe'
        db 'r makes bootable USB sticks; v2.9.15: the mouse no longer lags behind the hand; v2.9.14: the build signs the kernel as i'
        db 't is on the disk - update can replace it; v2.9.13: shared work can', 39, 't hang (solo after 5 s), update writes the kernel fir'
        db 'st and checks it; v2.9.12: the other cores get their caches on, help in pages, cores solo; v2.9.11: update from a USB st'
        db 'ick, restart fixed, one core by default; v2.9.10: the safe start, ', 39, 'cores one / all / beat', 39, '; v2.9.9: Photon from the desk'
        db 'top, the floor as a plane; v2.9.8: the Photon engine in the SUB-GPU; v2.9.7: the log ring; v2.9.6: Notepad, Console, sum'
        db 'mer time; v2.9.5: machine keys, the Sentinel checks the kernel; v2.9.4: Paint; v2.9.3: programs on every CPU core at onc'
        db 'e; v2.9.2: the Sentinel refuses changed objects, machine identity; v2.9: window buttons per app, minimise, DesktopStone,'
        db ' kill, NET, Chronos, the PC clock) (every program an .asmo, the kernel in .kasm parts, a system cabinet only the system '
        db 'reads, the stencil look: rounded see-through glass), a storage room of cabinets and drawers, RGBA identities, a split ke'
        db 'rnel, the Multiplexer (programs side by side in windows), system sockets, locked objects, PyTon (text, lists, dicts, flo'
        db 'ats, functions; compiled to native code inside NinuxOS), every CPU core, USB keyboards and mice (every xHCI controller, '
        db 'report-protocol mice; UHCI and OHCI too, v2.2), USB sticks on xHCI and EHCI, sound (HD Audio, AC97) and screen modes (v2'
        db '.3), the network and Meta Net with signed, encrypted pages (v2.4) with share / transfer / broadcast / subscribe (v2.5); '
        db 'kernel suits (KASM objects) put on when needed (v2.6), SATA (AHCI) and NVMe disks and an installer onto them, ACPI power'
        db '-off, a virtio-gpu driver and the GPU lab, a taskbar and Studio drawn as pages, memory and page tables per program with '
        db 'time slices (v2.1), apps, Studio, HTML + CSS pages with PyTon scripts, shield', 10, 0

